    "lawCode": "Amd §235, add §236-b, Pub Health L",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S4741\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act to amend the public health law, in relation\nto establishing a rural health council\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to amend the public health law to create a\nstatutory Rural Health Council within the Department of Health to\nadvise the Commissioner on all aspects of rural health care.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends section 235 of the public health law to\nhave the existing definition of the council reference section 2 of the\nbill.\n\nSection 2 of the bill adds a new section 236-b to establish the rural\nhealth council in with gubernatorial and legislative appointments.\nThe Council is charged with advising the Commissioner of Health on all\naspects of rural health care delivery as well as advocating for rural\nhealth care needs and assisting the Office of Rural Health with its\ndelineated responsibilities. Members must come from rural areas of the\nstate and have appropriate expertise. At least annually, the Council\nshall submit a report to the Regional Economic Development Councils\n(REDCs), on the status of the health care workforce supply in their\nregions. The Council shall meet as frequently as its business may\nrequire, but at least two times a year. Meetings may be called by the\nChairman or by the Commissioner. The meetings shall be live webcast\nand made available to the public. Members of the Council shall not\nreceive any compensation but be allowed their actual and necessary\nexpenses.\n\nSection 3 is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe current rural health council within the Department of health was\nestablished in 1988 with members appointed by the Governor. This\nlegislation seeks to focus the Councils efforts given significant\nchanges to the state's health care system and the challenges those\nchanges place on rural parts of our state.\n\nThe Council is best suited to provide guidance and expertise to the\nDepartment and the state in addressing the unique challenges for rural\nhealth care. This legislation places the Council in statute, adds\nlegislative appointments, connects the work of the Council to the\nRegional Economic Development Councils and ensures that the meetings\nof the Council are webcast and achieved by the Department, as are\nother meetings.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nThe Department of Health already holds and staffs rural council\nmeetings.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis bill is effective immediately.\n",
